ino being thunderspeared which was  one of the nicest shots to come out of  this episode and there were quite a few  as the camera moves towards the front  gate the yeager brothers do finally make  contact as aaron's severed head falls  into zeke's hand and because he's  technically alive in this moment the  founding titan has now been activated  the anime then shows us this amazing  montage of memories flashing in front of  aaron's eyes and these memories include  things from the future the past and even  from alternate realities the first  vision we see is one of mikasa and this  is likely a reinterpretation of this  scene from the very first episode when  she had just woken him up from a dream  although the anime version and the manga  versions of the stream were different  the fact is that in both cases aaron saw  at least one memory from the future and  in this episode that's about to happen  again  up next there's a vision of rhino when  he was in the cadets and this was the  moment when he told aaron to keep moving  forward that catchphrase has become one  of eren's driving motivations ever since  so it's understandable why this memory  shows up after this we see one of  grisha's memories and this was of his  sister faye before she was killed by  malian officials grisha's angered his  sister's death was a large reason why he  chose to join the aldian restorationist  which is effectively what led all the  main characters to where they are now  following faye's appearance aaron then  sees a memory of frieda rice brushing  her hair and this one is from back in  season 3. back when he was tied up in  the rice chapel he saw this same memory  of frida in her bedroom and for a split  second it seemed like she could see him  back  the memories then transitioned to one of  reiner begging erin to kill him to  another from his childhood when armin  was playfully running away going past  armin's hair we then see the main  members of the rice family and this  memory belongs to grisha an interesting  detail is that there are clouds in the  background to represent the paradise  this family had before grisha showed up  and the background changes to red to  represent him killing them it then  switches to different fragments from  aaron's past including an image of  captain levi sasha and connie messing  around when they were in the cadets and  falco coming to eren for advice when he  was undercover in mali one of the  easiest memories to miss though was this  one that belonged to kruger and this  showed up right after falco's appearance  although the anime brushes passed it  super quickly this memory was a lot  clearer in the manga version and it's of  the moment when krueger's parents and  sister were about to be set on fire as  he explained in his backstory his dad  was one of the original alden  restorationists and because of that  connection his family were killed by  marley while he could only watch on from  his hiding place in the closet the next  scene then gives us a stylized version  of berto's colossal titan appearing in  front of bulmaria before moving on to  what can only be described as reiner and  levi and some other guys in a sauna this  is a reference to the alternate cover  for volume 31 of the manga although why  it appears in eren's memories is a bit  of a mystery if if we assume that  something like this did actually happen  then i'm just having a hard time  figuring out where it fits on the  timeline since levi had no reason to  relax with these guys when they were  cadets and after they graduated i just  don't i don't really see levi being in a  sauna with reiner specifically that  being said it's clearly here for a  reason so i mean maybe i've missed  something so if you have a good idea of  what this is about then do let me know  in the comments below  up next we get a brief vision of ramsay  who is a character that hasn't been  introduced in the anime yet but without  getting into spoilers this boy is  someone who ever met during his time in  mali many months ago the camera then  pans into ramsey's eyes to reveal a  haunting image of grishaiger screaming  while on his knees and based on what  he's wearing this is from the day he  massacred the ryze family  things then turn upside down to show a  very large bird flying towards fort  salter and again i'm not going to give  away spoilers here but this is the  memory from the future that i was  talking about fort salte is a very  important location in the history of  this series and the bird in question has  significance too as its origin can be  traced back to earlier in this episode  the key to grisha's basement then  appears on screen and transitions us to  the final set of memories the first of  which is of historia in this scene she  and aaron were having a conversation  about the future of the island and the  future of the world and this took place  before he went rogue in mali  that we literally get goth mikasa and  nerdy armin from attack on titan's  school class in this alternate reality  all of the main cast have drastically  different lives with levi being a  janitor pique being a news reporter  while armin mikasa and pretty much  everyone else is either a teacher or a  student at the school despite having the  manga volumes myself i personally never  care that much about schoolcast although  i know some people probably do  but the fact they actually put this in  the anime is basically a confirmation of  the attack on titan multiverse  in the original chapter when aaron saw  these memory shards i mean these  alternate versions of armin and mikasa  can be seen but i'm just surprised that  this gag has now become like 200 canon  by appearing in the anime as well  the last two memories to show up is  firstly one of the ocean which has a lot  of significance to aaron for obvious  reasons and then there's a different  vision of emir fritz who was the  original founding titan  this memory of the miera is pretty  significant as the camera zooms in to  show a bright flash of white light which  turns out to be the coordinate the  coordinate is where the paths connecting  all ldns converge into one and from this  place all subjects of emir are connected  through these parts the various memories  of every subject can be accessed and if  the founding titan wants to she can  manipulate the coordinate to alter the  bodies and minds of these aliens as well  anyhow after aaron's memory slideshow is  finished he manifests directly in front  of it in the past dimension while hobo  zeke is chained up behind him the reason  zeke's hair is longer than normal is  because time passes differently in this  reality and from his perspective it felt  like years until aaron arrived due to  the large amount of time he spent  trapped here alone he began to learn  various things about the founder  including the fact that the sand they're  standing on can be used by amir to  create anything  not only did she use it to rebuild his  body from scratch a couple episodes ago  but for the last two thousand years  she's been in here moulding titans from  scratch whenever someone needed their  power  now in order to explain how zeke got the  upper hand against aaron it's first  important to understand how the founding  titan actually works  to put it simply anything the founding  titan does or anything the founding  titan can do is because the emir is in  the past dimension making it happen so  essentially if you control your mirror  then you control the founder  historically speaking those who've  possessed the coordinate inside them  have always had royal blood so they had  no problem accessing the past dimension  and telling yamir what to do  in aaron's case though since he's a  regular eldian he needed the assistance  of zeke to get here and now that they're  both here ymir gives zeke priority due  to his royal blood  unlike the rice family he's arrived in  parts without actually having the  coordinate inside him and therefore he  hasn't been tated by the vow to announce  war which only affects royals who have  the founding titan for that reason he's  free to command yamir to do literally  anything he wants hence why he made her  create these chains his goal was to make  aaron believe that he'd been trapped by  the voucher announced war and in this  way he could test if aaron was really on  his side when it came down to it aaron  did take the bait and refused to use him  his powers for the euthanization plan  proving in zeke's mind that his  suspicion was correct and his brother  had been brainwashed by their father  remember ever since zeke found out that  he had a younger brother he assumed that  they'd both been brainwashed to become  alien restorationists from his  perspective it was sarva that saved him  from this mindset and now here in this  scene he wants to be the person to save  aaron the first time they met zeke even  promised that one day he would do this  so this encounter in the past dimension  is really just them coming full circle  by commanding emir zeke uses the  founder's power to restrict aaron in  these chains and his goal is to convince  his brother to join him in saving the  world of course his version of saving  the world means sterilizing every aldian  so it will be interesting to see how he  tries to convince aaron to do that in  the next episode  anyway people that was my breakdown for  episode 19 of attack on titan season 4  but one thing i quickly wanted to  mention was the reason falco disobeyed  the beast titan's order and went after  porco i didn't find the right moment to  talk about this earlier but essentially  in the beginning he follows these  instructions to go after reiner but at  the last second he abandoned that  objective to go after galliard an  explanation for this is that although he  was given orders sometimes titan  instincts can take priority and we've  seen that happen before with this titan  back in season 2. therefore falco  choosing to go after galileo does make  sense since pogo was completely out in  the open ready to be eaten whereas rhino  was still protected by this layer of  armor on top of that a few minutes had  passed and zeke gave the original  instruction so you know it's feasible  that after a while the will to follow a  certain task can be more easily  forgotten those are just my thoughts in  it but let me know your opinion in the  comments down below and don't forget to  hit that sub button if you want to see  more videos like this  until the next one peace out
 

